ESLint v9 flat-config integration (REQ-ESLINT-COMPAT, REQ-CONFIG-SYSTEM):
- Root eslint.config.js is a flat config that loads the plugin dynamically and wires it into ESLint v9:
  - Dynamic plugin resolution from source or build:
    let plugin;
    try {
      plugin = require("./src/index.js");
    } catch (eSrc) {
      try {
        plugin = require("./lib/src/index.js");
      } catch (eLib) {
        const inCI = process.env.NODE_ENV === "ci" || process.env.CI === "true";
        if (inCI) {
          throw new Error(
            "Traceability plugin not found. Expected ./src/index.js or ./lib/src/index.js to be present in CI.",
          );
        } else {
          console.warn("Traceability plugin not built yet, skipping traceability rules");
          plugin = {};
        }
      }
    }
  - Integration into flat config blocks:
    module.exports = [
      js.configs.recommended,
      { ... },
      {
        files: ["tests/integration/cli-integration.test.ts"],
        languageOptions: { ... },
        plugins: { ...(plugin.rules ? { traceability: plugin } : {}) },
        rules: { complexity: "error" },
      },
      {
        files: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"],
        languageOptions: { parser: typescriptParser, parserOptions: { project: "./tsconfig.json", ... } },
        plugins: { ...(plugin.rules ? { traceability: plugin } : {}) },
        rules: { ... },
      },
      ...
    ];
- README.md documents ESLint v9 flat-config usage for users:
  - "Prerequisites: Node.js >=14 and ESLint v9+."
  - Example flat eslint.config.js with plugins: { traceability: {} } and traceability rules.
  - Quick Start using traceability.configs.recommended with an import of the plugin.

